  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Intransitive godan verb. Xが{高|たか}ぶる.\n\nDescribes emotions or nerves becoming heightened, often excitement or agitation. Frequently in the て-form ({高|たか}ぶって).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {気持|きも}ちが{高|たか}ぶる: to feel worked up\n- {神経|しんけい}が{高|たか}ぶる: to be on edge; nerves heightened\n- {感情|かんじょう}が{高|たか}ぶる: emotions run high\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {興奮|こうふん}する: to get excited — more general and neutral\n- {高揚|こうよう}する: to be elated, uplifted — positive, elevated mood",
